integ5 0083 = pdl5/slot4/0070-glm-pdl-moe-router-glue.patch (overnight 2026-10-31), renumbered for the integrated stack on 3f94715d.

pdl5 0070 (c3, rebased for integ5's order: after graph5 0068, before attn5 0069): a decode window's MoE router glue as
dependents (TF_GLM_PDL_CHAIN's moe, in the default; TF_GLM_PDL_CHAIN=reduce,hc,p2p is the same binary without it).
- glm_glue_bmm.cuh: tf_glm_router_tile (an ordinary launch) triggers its dependents first.
- glm_glue_moe.cuh: glue5's fused tf_glm_topk_group_sum stages the bias (immutable) into shared memory, then waits
  (the router's slices are an earlier grid's), then triggers; every store after the wait. The fallback
  tf_glm_topk_group waits first, then triggers.
- glm_glue_rows.cuh: tf_glm_slice_sum (the DSA index gate's and the fallback's) waits first, then triggers.
- cuda_glue.zig: Set.pdl_moe; topk_group_sum, topk_group and slice_sum launch with it. cuda_forward.zig: decode
  windows only. cuda_mm.zig: Chain.moe (in Chain.all). glm_mm_policy_host.zig: its parse cases.
The EXL3 kernels after the select stay ordinary launches (the common EXL3 module is untouched). Exact by
construction: the same kernels and arithmetic, every read of another grid's data after its wait.

